\f0\fs24 \cf0 # ADR-001: Modular Monolith Architecture\
\
## Status\
\
Accepted\
\
## Context\
\
The BitePlate Smart Restaurant Management System requires multiple business domains including reservations, orders, kitchen management, billing, notifications, and order history.\
\
A microservice architecture was considered, but it would significantly increase deployment complexity, service discovery requirements, network communication, distributed transactions, and infrastructure management.\
\
The project is developed by a single developer and is intended as an educational and portfolio project.\
\
## Decision\
\
The system will use a Modular Monolith architecture.\
\
Each business domain will be implemented as an independent module within a single Spring Boot application.\
\
Examples:\
\
- Reservation Module\
- Order Module\
- Kitchen Module\
- Billing Module\
- Notification Module\
\
Each module will have its own package structure and business logic while sharing the same deployment and database.\
\
## Consequences\
\
Advantages:\
\
- Simpler deployment\
- Easier debugging\
- Better maintainability\
- Clear separation of concerns\
- Easy migration to microservices in the future\
\
Disadvantages:\
\
- Shared database\
- Single deployment unit\
- Less independent scalability than microservices\
\
## Justification\
\
A Modular Monolith provides an excellent balance between enterprise architecture principles and practical project complexity.}